[
    {
        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39113\">#39113</a>, the <code>simpNF</code> linter is complaining, and I think it's right and <code>simp</code> is doing something weird. MWE on master:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">integrable_zero_vectorMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">VectorMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Integrable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">VectorMeasure</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Integrable</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The <code>simpNF</code> linter complains that <code>simp</code> can prove the lemma by itself. But <code>:= by simp</code> doesn't work, so it looks like the <code>simpNF</code> linter is crazy. Except that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Integrable#doc\">docs#MeasureTheory.VectorMeasure.Integrable</a> is an abbrev, so it should be completely transparent to <code>simp</code> and it should not be needed in the above <code>simp</code> call, and it looks like <code>simpNF</code> is correct, and <code>simp</code> is mistaken.</p>\n<p>As to why <code>simp</code> and <code>simpNF</code> have different opinions here, I have no clue...</p>",
        "id": 599096050,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780302166
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems to be the wrong PR number?</p>",
        "id": 599096450,
        "sender_full_name": "Rémy Degenne",
        "timestamp": 1780302280
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It should be <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39113\">#39113</a> I guess</p>",
        "id": 599096882,
        "sender_full_name": "Rémy Degenne",
        "timestamp": 1780302420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are two things going on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When we say that an abbrev is transparent to <code>simp</code>, we mean that while trying a rewrite, the abbrev is unfolded if necessary. However, <code>simp</code> only tries to rewrite in positions that exist in the original expression. In your example, <code>simp</code> needs to rewrite with <code>VectorMeasure.transpose_zero_vectorMeasure</code> in a subexpression that doesn't exist until we unfold <code>VectorMeasure.Integrable</code>.</li>\n<li>It looks like the preprocessing of <code>simpNF</code> runs <code>whnfR</code> on the LHS before simplifying it. (I haven't found the precise cause yet). This looks like a bug to me.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 599143236,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780316379
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have now a PR, ready for review, at <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/40198\">#40198</a>, where the issue shows up. For now I have nolinted the offending declarations, but I'm not sure that's an optimal solution.</p>",
        "id": 599900035,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780515512
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I looked into it deeper, and it's actually worse than I thought. <code>simpNF</code> is not at fault - it is faithfully copying what <code>simp</code> does. The problem is that <code>@[simp]</code> is not creating the simp lemma that you think it is creating.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MeasureTheory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MeasurableSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedAddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">NormedSpace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">integrable_zero_vectorMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">VectorMeasure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">F</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Integrable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">VectorMeasure</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Integrable</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- This is the lemma that will be used by `simp`:</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- It, in fact, can be solved with simp.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">auxLemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">info: MeasureTheory.integrable_zero_vectorMeasure._simp_1.{u_1, u_2, u_3, u_4} {X : Type u_1} {E : Type u_2} {F : Type u_3}</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  {G : Type u_4} [MeasurableSpace X] [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F]</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  [NormedAddCommGroup G] [NormedSpace ℝ G] {f : X → E} {B : E →L[ℝ] F →L[ℝ] G} :</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Integrable f (VectorMeasure.transpose 0 B).variation = True</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">integrable_zero_vectorMeasure</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">simp_1</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599939080,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780525504
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Looks like a bug in <code>simp</code>, right? mwe:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myDef</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">myAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">auxLemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: foo._simp_1 (f : Nat) : myDef f = True -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"bp\">._</span><span class=\"n\">simp_1</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600057858,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780570788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't think I am convinced that <code>simp</code> is at fault here given the discussion so far. The auxiliary <code>_simp_*</code> declarations are internal helper constants; the <code>simpNF</code> linter shouldn't rely on them being in a specific form or existing at all.</p>",
        "id": 600618114,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1780647703
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree that the auxiliary lemma created by <code>simp</code> does its job, i.e., it will simplify the expression as requested (because at this point simp will see through the abbrev). I wonder if that's fixable on the <code>simpNF</code> side.</p>",
        "id": 600622612,
        "sender_full_name": "Sébastien Gouëzel",
        "timestamp": 1780648695
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I suppose the fix for simpNF is to copy-paste the implementation of simp's pre-processor, and tweak it slightly so that it doesn't run <code>whnf</code> on the conclusion. This is a bit annoying though.</p>",
        "id": 600622888,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780648762
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems to me that, <code>@[simp]</code> theorems whose <code>conclusion</code> is an application of a reducible definition of an equality <code>a = b</code>, will generally fail to be applied to the definition by <code>simp</code>, since <code>simp</code> will only try to rewrite <code>a</code> to <code>b</code> instead of rewriting the whole <code>a = b</code> to <code>True</code>.</p>\n<p>MWE:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Semireducible definition of an equality. `@[simp]` theorems will work well.</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne_lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne_lemma</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOne</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">section</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- reducible definition of an equality.</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- or `abbrev SqEqOneAbbrev (a : Nat) := a ^ 2 = 1`</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- A `@[simp]` theorem whose conclusion is the definition holds on a specific argument.</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: `simp` made no progress</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- `SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma` doesn't work because `simp` only tries to rewrite LHS `n ^ 2` to RHS `1`?</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: `simp` made no progress</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- same</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works if the definition is unfolded</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- it will work since `simp` will not try to rewrite the LHS `n ^ 2`</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev_lemma'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hn</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SqEqOneAbbrev</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
